Point the kernel build at the pahole copy from dev-util/pahole-cachyos,
which carries the merged-CU --lang_exclude fixes (lore v2 series) needed
by Rust + LTO + BTF builds. dev-util/pahole stays untouched and both can
be installed side by side.

PAHOLE uses ?= (same style as ARCH/KBUILD_IMAGE in this Makefile), so an
externally supplied PAHOLE — make command line or environment — always
wins over this default. The default is an absolute path on purpose:
kbuild resolves $(PAHOLE) once via scripts/pahole-version.sh during
olddefconfig, and an absolute path lets external modules built against
/usr/src/linux-* pick the same binary without any PATH tricks. If
pahole-cachyos is removed, BTF generation silently turns off
(pahole-version.sh prints 0); it never breaks the build.

Applies to every 6.18/7.x tree shipping the standard PAHOLE line in the
top-level Makefile (~line 539). Trees without BINDGEN right above it
(6.12 and older) apply with a one-line offset.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -536,7 +536,7 @@
 RUSTFMT		= rustfmt
 CLIPPY_DRIVER	= clippy-driver
 BINDGEN		= bindgen
-PAHOLE		= pahole
+PAHOLE		?= /usr/libexec/pahole-cachyos/bin/pahole
 RESOLVE_BTFIDS	= $(objtree)/tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/resolve_btfids
 LEX		= flex
 YACC		= bison
